// The ShapesDemo type of ../ShapeType.idl, for OpenDDS's IDL compiler.
//
// `@must_understand` on the key member is what XTypes 1.3 §7.2.2.4.4.4.8
// makes implicit ("key members shall always have their 'must understand'
// attribute set to true"). ZeroDDS and Cyclone DDS set IS_MUST_UNDERSTAND
// on a key member without it; opendds_idl 3.34 sets it only when the
// annotation is written (dds/idl/typeobject_generator.cpp), so the two
// minimal TypeObjects differ in that one flag and their hashes differ.
// OpenDDS 3.34 also numbers TypeConsistencyKind from 1
// (DdsDcpsCore.idl: DISALLOW_TYPE_COERCION = 1, ALLOW_TYPE_COERCION = 2)
// where XTypes 1.3 numbers it from 0, reads a remote reader's
// ALLOW_TYPE_COERCION as DISALLOW, and then matches only identical type
// identifiers. Written out, the flag gives OpenDDS the TypeObject the
// specification asks for, and the identifiers agree.
@topic
@final
struct ShapeType {
  @key @must_understand string color;
  long x;
  long y;
  long shapesize;
};
